            <div xml:id="d772">

                <pb facs="0828" n="724" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg724"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Manchuria/151: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland (Wilson)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-04-25T18:00:00-04:00">April 25, 1932—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>57. For the Secretary of State. In reply to special inquiry by Department
                    regarding items reported concerning Ohashi, until recently Japanese Consul
                    General at Harbin, Legation, Peiping, telegraphs under date April 25: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Ohashi will be in charge of general affairs in the Foreign Office at
                            Changchun. In this capacity the foreign affairs of the new government
                            will practically be in his hands.”</p></quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
